## Primitives in the hydra.core.lib.pairs module.
##
## Pairs: the two-component product type. This module provides the two projections, the bifunctor map, and the constructor.
module hydra.core.lib.pairs



## Map over both elements of a pair.
##
## bimap(f, g, p) returns a new pair (f(first(p)), g(second(p))). The bifunctor map for pairs.
## Total. Corresponds to Haskell's Data.Bifunctor.bimap :: (a -> c) -> (b -> d) -> (a, b) -> (c, d).
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement mapsBothElementsIndependently: bimap applies the first function to the pair's first element and the second function to the pair's second element, producing a new pair of the two results, for any element and function types.
primitive bimap : ∀a,b,c,d.(a → c) → (b → d) → (a, b) → (c, d) = λf.λg.λp.(f (hydra.core.lib.pairs.first p), g (hydra.core.lib.pairs.second p))

## Get the first element of a pair.
##
## first(p) returns the first component of the pair p.
## Total. Corresponds to Haskell's fst :: (a, b) -> a.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement returnsFirstComponent: first returns the first component of the pair unchanged, for any element type and value.
primitive first : ∀a,b.(a, b) → a

## Construct a pair from two values.
##
## pair(x, y) returns the pair (x, y).
## The type-free pair constructor, useful point-free (e.g. zipWith(pair, xs, ys)).
## Total. Corresponds to Haskell's (,) :: a -> b -> (a, b).
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement constructsFromTwoValues: pair x y constructs the pair (x, y), preserving both components exactly as given, for any value.
primitive pair : ∀a,b.a → b → (a, b)

## Get the second element of a pair.
##
## second(p) returns the second component of the pair p.
## Total. Corresponds to Haskell's snd :: (a, b) -> b.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement returnsSecondComponent: second returns the second component of the pair unchanged, for any element type and value.
primitive second : ∀a,b.(a, b) → b